Description: avfilter/tonemap_cuda: keep a sample on a pivot in the piece that starts there
 The reshape kernel reads a 10-bit sample from a 16-bit texture and
 rescales it in float32. For some codes, 545 among them, the result is
 one ulp below the pivot of the same code, which is stored as
 code * (1.0f / 1023). A sample on such a pivot took the piece before.
 tonemapx divides each sample by 1023 and is not affected.
 .
 Store each inner pivot 2^-21 lower. That is 8 ulps at 0.5, above the
 rounding of the read, and far below the 1/1023 between two 10-bit
 codes. Chroma that the texture filters to less than 2^-21 below a
 pivot, a two-thousandth of a code, now takes the piece above too.
 Filtered chroma can come as close to a pivot as the read rounds, so no
 margin separates every such value from a rounded read of the pivot.
 .
 On a synthetic profile 5 picture with patches on four chroma pivots,
 all 12 patches on a pivot took the piece below before this patch, up
 to 16 chroma codes off, and none after. On that picture only samples
 that read exactly a pivot code change.
